# Integer128 minimum and maximum values

Binds the int128 maximum as a literal and derives the minimum by
subtracting one from the largest negative literal, because a negated
minimum-magnitude literal is validated unsigned first, consistent with
int8 and int64.

>>> source
ceiling: int128 = 170141183460469231731687303715884105727
floor: int128 = -170141183460469231731687303715884105727
unit: int128 = 1

// Verifies the largest int128 literal prints unchanged.
print(ceiling)

// Verifies the int128 minimum is reachable through checked arithmetic.
minimum: int128 = floor - unit
print(minimum)

<<< stdout
170141183460469231731687303715884105727
-170141183460469231731687303715884105728

<<< stderr
